    "assistant_text": "Confirming: computing the discount per-line-item and summing gives 105.66 (932+3522+6112 cents), producing a total due of 1324.84 \u2014 one cent off from the test's 1324.83. Computing the discount once on the subtotal gives 105.67, producing 1324.83 exactly, which matches what the test expects. So the bug is in `engine.settle()`: it should round the discount once on the subtotal, not per line item.\nNow let me run the test suite to confirm.\nAll 6 tests pass. The fix: `engine.settle()` was rounding the promotional discount per line item and summing the rounded results, which accumulates rounding drift (three separate half-up roundings instead of one). Computing the discount once on the invoice subtotal fixes the one-cent gap.\n\nNote `src/ledger/rules.py` still has an uncommitted, unrelated `LATE_FEE_RATE`/`late_fee_for()` addition (not wired into settlement) \u2014 leaving that as-is since it wasn't part of this bug.",
